#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
dtRadio — Vintage HF/Shortwave, Amateur Repeater, NOAA, Emergency & Space Receiver for CDE

Features:
  - Authentic 1980s/1990s communications receiver faceplate styled for CDE (OSF/Motif bevels):
      * Warm backlit ballistic Analog S-Meter (S1..S9 +20 +40 +60 dB) driven by live audio/RF
      * Glowing cyan-green Vacuum Fluorescent Display (VFD) + scrolling vernier dial scale
      * Weighted spun-aluminum VFO tuning flywheel (drag or scroll wheel)
      * 6 interactive rotary DSP knobs: AF GAIN, RF GAIN, SQUELCH, CLARIFIER, IF WIDTH, TONE/NB
      * Hardware switches: NB (Noise Blanker), ANL (Voice Limiter), CLAR, ATT (-12dB), AGC, LOCK, MUTE, REC
  - Direct Safety-Orange [FEMA / EMERG] button (Emergency audio + live OpenFEMA & NWS CAP alerts)
  - Direct NOAA-Blue [NOAA WX] button (24/7 live NOAA Weather Radio All-Hazards transmitters)
  - Live 0-30 MHz off-air HF/Shortwave reception via the public KiwiSDR network (WebSocket PCM/ADPCM)
  - Curated non-music station banks (HF Time/Utility, Ham Bands & CW, Shortwave Relays, NOAA, Emergency/Scanners, Space)
  - 12-channel Memory Bank (M01-M12): short-click to recall, press-and-hold (0.65s) to store favorite
  - Built-in plug-and-play USB RTL-SDR hardware support (`rtl_fm` 24-1766 MHz) ready when a dongle is connected
"""

